{
  "_doc": [
    "Frozen test-only corpus (#139E M12.4): EVERY currently-canonical NON-listener",
    "sync_pipeline chain, plus one verb-casing duplicate. No production code path",
    "reads this file.",
    "",
    "It is the SINGLE definition of 'which chains are canonical', shared by",
    "tests/test_process_emitter_parity.py (the adapter-dialect parity harness) and",
    "tests/test_sync_pipeline_adapter_cutover.py (the differential cut-over oracle), so",
    "the two suites cannot drift apart on the question.",
    "",
    "COVERAGE IS DERIVED, NOT ENUMERATED -- and this doc deliberately states no case",
    "COUNT, because a count here could only go stale.",
    "",
    "test_sync_corpus_covers_every_canonical_chain READS the builder's accepted",
    "stage-kind sequences out of its own source (the `if kinds not in (...)` literal in",
    "lower_config, extracted by AST), enumerates every primitive assignment over them",
    "from _SYNC_PIPELINE_STAGE_PRIMITIVE / _SYNC_PIPELINE_STAGE_ALT_PRIMITIVE, and lets",
    "the routing gate split the results into canonical / legacy-arm. This corpus must",
    "then cover exactly the canonical ones. A new stage kind, a new primitive, or a",
    "newly permitted stage SEQUENCE therefore fails the suite until this file grows.",
    "Do not re-freeze this as a hand-maintained list.",
    "",
    "Case names ARE the fingerprint: <source_primitive>[_map]_<target_primitive>, so an",
    "omission is visible by inspection. `soap_lowercase_execute` is the single sanctioned",
    "duplicate fingerprint -- the non-uppercase `execute` verb the pre-#139C canonicalizer",
    "corrupted.",
    "",
    "WHY IT READS THE GRAMMAR INSTEAD OF MODELLING IT -- three fail-open holes, each",
    "found by grading the UNIVERSE rather than reading the artifact, and each time the",
    "MODEL was the defect rather than its parameters:",
    "",
    "  1. The first draft froze #139C's inline set: 6 stage-kind chains, which at the",
    "     primitive level covered well under half the canonical universe, omitting the",
    "     map-ful SOAP chain and every mixed-connector-family combination -- precisely",
    "     the surface the #139A cross-role connector guard and #139C's own",
    "     family-conditional canonicalizer defect live on. (Live QA.)",
    "  2. The fix still MODELLED the grammar as source x target x +/-map, classifying",
    "     kinds by the adapter's role sets; a kind in BOTH sets was filed source-only,",
    "     so giving `fetch` a target role and permitting `read -> fetch` made",
    "     db_read_rest_fetch reachable, canonical and uncovered, all guards green.",
    "     (Codex impl-vs-plan review.)",
    "  3. Dropping the role model left an ARITY model. Fixed lengths {2,3} missed a",
    "     permitted 4-stage fetch->map->map->send -- four canonical chains that are",
    "     byte-DISTINCT (both map stages dropped, zero map shapes emitted) with parity",
    "     still holding, because canonical and legacy drop them identically. Replacing",
    "     the fixed lengths with a sweep-until-a-length-is-dry was STILL a model:",
    "     dryness is local, so a grammar accepting 5-stage chains while 4 stays dry is",
    "     missed entirely. (Live QA, both.)",
    "",
    "  4. Reading the grammar by AST was a fourth model -- a SYNTAX model. It searched",
    "     for a comparison that looked right and skipped anything else, so EXTENDING the",
    "     guard stayed invisible while the match count held at 1: hoisting the tuple into",
    "     a module constant, or adding `and len(kinds) != 5`, both evaded it. It now",
    "     anchors on the guard STATEMENT and refuses any test it cannot read. (Live QA.)",
    "",
    "No bounded sampling of the chain space is complete against a grammar that can",
    "change shape. Hence: read the grammar -- but see THE HONEST LIMIT in",
    "_sync_probe_chain_space's docstring, which records TWO residual classes that must",
    "not be conflated. (a) The EXTRACTION class: an AST pattern cannot be a completeness",
    "oracle, so the tightening buys fail-closed, not proof; hoisting the tuple to a module",
    "constant in process_flow_builder and importing it WOULD remove this class (~3 lines of",
    "production change, hence not in #139E, and recorded in the ledger as the intended",
    "resolution for the next slice touching that file). (b) The BYPASS class, which",
    "hoisting does NOT touch: an acceptance path that never mentions `kinds` is invisible",
    "to any reading of the grammar statement -- measured, the extraction returns the",
    "byte-identical sequences under such a bypass, so an imported constant would too. Its",
    "only detector is the bounded behavioural cross-check, and no bound closes it.",
    "",
    "`name`/`folder_name`/`anchor` are case METADATA, deliberately siblings of `config`",
    "and never inside it: SyncPipelineBuilder.lower_config drops name/folder_name",
    "(process_flow_builder.py:5497-5499) and adapt_sync_pipeline's _KNOWN_ROOT_KEYS",
    "would reject them if they ever did survive.",
    "",
    "The cases carrying an `anchor` reproduce a committed raw-byte golden under",
    "tests/fixtures/golden_xml/ -- generated through the LEGACY renderer before the",
    "#139C cut-over, so they are not self-confirming. Their name/folder_name MUST stay",
    "byte-exact or the anchored assertion is meaningless. The rest are pinned by the",
    "differential oracle alone.",
    "",
    "The WSS listener chains are NOT here: their fused `start_listen` entry has no",
    "registry key, so they stay on the legacy renderer. The coverage test still GENERATES",
    "them as candidates and asserts the gate routes them to the legacy arm -- so when #140",
    "lands start_listen and they become canonical, that test fails until this corpus grows."
  ],
